[
    {
        "content": "<p>Starting from this context:</p>\n<p><strong>I X</strong> : Type<br>\n<strong>A</strong> : I → Set X<br>\n<strong>f</strong> : I → ℕ<br>\n<strong>hf</strong> : Function.Injective f<br>\n<strong>gA✝</strong> : ∀ (i : I), ∃ f, Function.Injective f<br>\n<strong>gA</strong> : (i : I) → ↑(A i) ↪ ℕ<br>\n<strong>idx</strong> : ↑(⋃ i, A i) → I<br>\n<strong>hidx</strong> : ∀ (a : ↑(⋃ i, A i)), ↑a ∈ A (idx a)<br>\n<strong>s</strong> : ↑(⋃ i, A i) → ℕ × ℕ := fun a ↦ (f (idx a), (gA (idx a)) ⟨↑a, ⋯⟩)<br>\n<strong>a b</strong> : ↑(⋃ i, A i)<br>\n<strong>hfab</strong> : idx a = idx b<br>\n<strong>h1</strong> : ↑a ∈ A (idx a)<br>\n<strong>h2</strong> : ↑b ∈ A (idx b)<br>\n<strong>hgab</strong> : (gA (idx a)) ⟨↑a, h1⟩ = (gA (idx b)) ⟨↑b, h2⟩<br>\n<strong>⊢</strong> a = b</p>\n<p>I noticed that I couldn't use <code>rw [hfab] at *</code> to apply the equality everywhere (allowing me to use injectivity, grind, etc., beside the point). </p>\n<p>But it turns out the following <em>does</em> work:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">generalize</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">idx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span>\n<span class=\"n\">generalize</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">idx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span>\n<span class=\"n\">subst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hfab</span>\n<span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">gA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">injective</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hgab</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- This line isn't the focus but it does close the goal</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I'm trying to understand <em>why</em> this works. </p>\n<p>I somewhat understand why <code>rw</code> doesn't work: if I try to just <code>rw [hfab] at hgab</code>, I get a motive issue, because <code>hgab</code> is dependent on <code>h2</code>, which involves <code>idx b</code>. So, the state is weird and ill-formed without rewriting both. </p>\n<p>But I don't know exactly why <code>subst</code> succeeds where <code>rw [hfab] at *</code> doesn't. Does the latter rewrite sequentially, while <code>subst</code> does it simultaneously? If so, how does <code>subst</code> do it simultaneously? Is there an implementation-significant reason why this only works for the variable-elimination procedure (i.e. is the variable-elimination part of the reason these two work differently?)</p>",
        "id": 631463048,
        "sender_full_name": "Shaunticlair Ruiz",
        "timestamp": 1791929767
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The key is that <code>generalize idx a = i at *</code> rewrites <code>idx a = i</code> at <code>h1</code> and <code>hgab</code>  simultaneously. Substituting equations like <code>i = j</code> (where one is a variable) is on the other hand quite easy, in fact it will almost always work. But here's <em>how</em> it works:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">gA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↑</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↪</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">idx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↑</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">⋃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↑</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">⋃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hfab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">idx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">idx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↑</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">idx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↑</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">idx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hgab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">gA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">idx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨↑</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h1</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">gA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">idx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨↑</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h2</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">generalize</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">idx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">generalize</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">idx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- revert everything that depends on `j` (including `j` and the equality)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">revert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hgab</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">revert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h2</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">revert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hfab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- this one second-to-last</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">revert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- this one last</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- this puts our goal in the shape `∀ (j : I), i = j → p j`</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- now we have a lemma that `(∀ (j : I), i = j → p j) ↔ p i`</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">forall_eq'</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- finally, we can reintroduce `h2` and `hgab`</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hgab</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The <code>subst</code> tactic first reverts all variables that depends on <code>j</code> and <code>j</code> itself in such a way that the goal ends up in the shape <code>∀ (j : I), i = j → p j</code>. Then we can perform the substitution all at once using the lemma <code>forall_eq'</code> (the <code>subst</code> tactic uses something slightly different but equivalent). Finally we just introduce all the variables to put them back as hypotheses. As you can tell, the result of <code>subst hfab</code> is equivalent to doing this <code>revert</code> /  <code>rw</code> / <code>intro</code> pattern and works very generally for <code>variable = term</code> as long as <code>term</code> doesn't depend on <code>variable</code>.</p>\n<p>But I should maybe also say that whenever <code>rw</code> fails for \"motive is not type correct\" errors (you may not have seen them with <code>at *</code> but <code>rw [hfab] at hgab</code> should fail with such an error), you should try <code>rw!</code>. Indeed, <code>rw! [hfab] at *</code> <em>does</em> seem to work in your case.</p>",
        "id": 631468232,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1791931607
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, that makes sense, I think? So the <code>revert</code> operations fold everything into a single expression, and since <code>i=j</code> lives at the top of that structure, everything below it can be abstracted into <code>p j</code>. And turning <code>idx b</code> into <code>j</code> gives us an easy-identified variable to substitute, rather than an expression (strictly necessary for <code>forall_eq'</code> or <code>subst</code>). Whereas <code>rw</code> only does one expression at a time.</p>\n<p>Though, that <em>is</em> interesting, it does seem that <code>rw!</code> is strong enough to resolve it:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">rw!</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">hfab</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span>\n<span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">gA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">idx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">injective</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hgab</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Though I'm not quite sure why adding <code>dsimp</code> allows it to do that. I guess I've got the hint from the motive error message:</p>\n<p><code>...or use 'simp' or 'conv' mode, which have strategies for certain kinds of dependencies...</code></p>\n<p>Thank you for the suggestion of <code>rw!</code>, it'll probably make some situations I would've previously managed with <code>conv</code> or <code>generalize_proofs</code> or other shenanigans, more straightforward.</p>",
        "id": 631477135,
        "sender_full_name": "Shaunticlair Ruiz",
        "timestamp": 1791935668
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note you're not meant to meet such trouble. This is very probably a consequence of unfortunate design choices.</p>",
        "id": 631546756,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1791959894
    }
]